## Install

1. Drop the `Scripts/` folder into your project's `Assets/` and the
   `Resources/` folder's contents into your project's `Assets/Resources/`
   (the pipeline's `unity-create` overlay step does this automatically for a
   composed project — see `Assets/Resources/Sprites/{{ s.entity_name }}/`).
2. Add the `{{ s.name }}` component to the `{{ s.entity_name }}` GameObject —
   it requires a `SpriteRenderer` on the same object.

## Behaviour

Loads every generated frame via `Resources.LoadAll<Sprite>()` at `Awake()`.
Idle{% if "run" in actions %}/run{% endif %}{% if "jump" in actions %}/jump{% endif %} state is inferred each frame from the
GameObject's own motion (no dependency on any specific controller script — it
reads `transform.position` deltas directly, so it works with any movement
code). One-shot actions
({% for a in actions if a not in ("idle", "run", "jump") %}{{ a }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})
are triggered from elsewhere via:

```csharp
SendMessage("PlayAction", "punch_light", SendMessageOptions.DontRequireReceiver);
```

with no compile-time reference needed — Controller.cs.j2 and Health.cs.j2
already call this at the right moments (attack/jump/hurt/death) when a
sprite-animated entity is composed alongside them.

## Art generation

Frames were generated once via a local ComfyUI server and frozen to
`Resources/Sprites/{{ s.entity_name }}/<action>/frame_NN.png` — see
`Resources/sprite_manifest.json` for exactly what was generated vs.
placeholder-filled (a solid magenta frame means ComfyUI was unreachable or a
specific frame failed; re-run sprite generation once that's fixed, it will
not silently pass off a placeholder as real art).
